<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle sell $101-$102/dressed-private.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle sell $101-$102/dressed-private.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nebraska feedlot cattle near midday Tuesday sold at $101.00 to $102.00 per cwt on a dressed basis in moderate volume, down $1.00 to $2.00 from the bulk of last week's top price, market sources said.</p>
<p>About 10,000 to 12,000 head sold, with further bids at $101.00 passed by several owners pricing cattle at $102.00 to $103.00, the sources said.</p>
<p>There were no reported sales on a live basis, with owners asking $63.00 following thin sales on Monday at $62.00.</p>
<p>Fed cattle prices were pressured by spillover weakness from the southern plains and weak beef values, they said.</p>
<p>((Bob Janis 312-983-7347))</p>
